  "notes": "Defect-type tally for the baseline window, transcribed daily from the QC desk reject log (paper, both shifts) -- entry_mode 'transcribed' with count carrying that shift's tally marks for that check, which is the honest path for a paper tally and is excluded from the burst-entry heuristic by design. Tally rule from the collection plan: ONE MARK PER FAILED CHECK, so an order failing two checks carries two marks -- the window holds 139 marks on 135 rejected orders (4 orders failed two checks). Categories are exactly the four named checks; the export feeds the engine Pareto with zero re-typing (to-dataset), and the same table cut by the shift stratum is the chi-square screen's input.",
